# ect-core

> Compute-time-backed token boilerplate on the Bitcoin Core integration/staging tree.

## Purpose
Explain ect-core as a token sketch tied to compute time, sitting on a Bitcoin Core staging tree. Source: fitzyracing1/ect-core.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Start from the Bitcoin Core integration/staging tree.
2. Treat compute time as the backing idea for the token.
3. Keep this repo as boilerplate, not a live coin.

## Key ideas
- Compute-time-backed (time spent computing as the named backing)
- Token boilerplate (a starter, not a launched coin)
- Bitcoin Core staging tree (the code base it sits on)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/ect-core
tree = bitcoin_core_staging()
token = compute_time_backed(tree)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. bitcoin_core_staging() → “use that tree as the base”
2. compute_time_backed(tree) → “name compute time as the backing idea”

## Decisions the program makes
- If someone treats this as a live coin → correct: it is boilerplate
- If compute time is missing → the backing idea is empty

## What a person would notice
A token sketch on a Core tree, not an exchange listing.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the source and read the boilerplate.
